{% # theme-check-disable %}
{%- comment -%}
  Only the body font is preloaded. Every font uses font-display: swap, so none of them block text
  from showing; preloading all four (~140KB) just competed with the hero image (the mobile LCP) for
  bandwidth on slow connections. The subheading / heading / accent fonts load from their
  @font-face rules as soon as text needs them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%} Not on the homepage: its @font-face rules load after the hero paints (snippets/theme-styles-variables.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless settings.type_body_font.system? or template.name == 'index' and request.design_mode == false -%}
  <link
    rel="preload"
    as="font"
    href="{{ settings.type_body_font | font_url }}"
    type="font/woff2"
    crossorigin
    fetchpriority="low"
  >
{%- endunless -%}
{% # theme-check-enable %}

{%- comment -%}
  Poppins (Google Fonts) and Clash Grotesk (Fontshare) used to load here on every page.
  The site's fonts come from Theme settings > Typography (Inter / Manrope), which override
  base.css's Poppins, so Poppins was unused. Clash Grotesk is only used by the updates-grid
  section, which now loads it itself.
{%- endcomment -%}
